  "context": "PR #2894 remains open on branch fix/throughput-stream-count-derived. Oracle findings were addressed: corpus and Explorer mismatch helpers now apply only to COMPLETED throughput phases, so FAILED/PARTIAL truncation is neither a corpus hard error nor mislabeled count exclusion. Coverage includes run.streams/config.streams and FAILED/PARTIAL; hosted-results docs state the status boundary. Verification after fix: 328 focused tests; standalone smoke confirmed corpus acceptance of a failed 2-of-3 bundle and Explorer preservation of `missing_primary_metric`; `make ci-docs` passed; comment-policy passed (0 violations, 19 native checks); Ruff format/check and `git diff --check` passed. Explicit-file commit command is running its hook in background job bg_60. Oracle review threads remain unresolved pending push/new review: `PRRT_kwDOQ7J64c6rHcEX` (corpus hard-fail) and `PRRT_kwDOQ7J64c6rHcEZ` (mislabeling). After commit hook succeeds, push branch, update PR #2894, resolve addressed threads, and require current-head Oracle success plus required CI before arming. No changes to unrelated PR #2835 paths.",
